# Requirements Document

## Domain Requirements

### DR-01: VST3 Plugin Development
The playbook must produce working VST3 audio plugins that:
- Load in REAPER DAW on Linux Mint
- Process or generate audio correctly
- Have functional modern UI
- Save and load presets
- Pass audio thread safety validation
- Handle sample rates 44.1kHz - 192kHz
- Handle buffer sizes 64 - 2048 samples

### DR-02: Sound Design Integration
The playbook must bridge subjective sound descriptors to technical parameters:
- Translate "warm", "bright", "lush", "psychedelic" to filter cutoff ranges, saturation amounts
- Provide preset creation methodology
- Support synthesis types: subtractive, FM, wavetable, granular, additive

### DR-03: Commercial Readiness
The playbook must produce plugins ready for commercial distribution:
- Licensing system integration
- Marketplace listing preparation
- Pricing strategy documentation
- Marketing timeline execution

### DR-04: Knowledge Base Architecture
The playbook must specify a multi-layer KB:
- **Technical Layer:** C++17, JUCE, CMake, DSP, audio thread safety
- **Sound Design Layer:** Synthesis theory, patch methodology, creative techniques
- **UI/UX Layer:** Audio plugin interface standards, control layout, visual design
- **Commercial Layer:** Marketplaces, licensing, pricing, marketing
- **Reference Layer:** Academic sources, textbooks, expert material
- **Bridge Layer:** Subjective-to-parameter translation

## Quality Requirements

### QR-01: Audio Thread Safety
- No allocations in processBlock()
- No locks in audio thread
- Lock-free inter-thread communication
- Parameter smoothing on all modulatable parameters

### QR-02: Code Quality
- CMake-based build with FetchContent
- Catch2 unit tests for DSP modules
- pluginval validation passing
- No static mutable state across instances

### QR-03: User Experience
- Professional UI following audio plugin standards
- Intuitive control layout
- Proper gain staging (effects audible at all parameter ranges)
- Preset system with meaningful names

### QR-04: Documentation
- All code reviewed for audio thread safety
- DSP algorithms documented with math
- Prevention rules from failure modes
- Session boundary documentation

## Strategic Requirements

### SR-01: Budget Compliance
- Claude AI: $200/month maximum
- Prefer free/open-source tools
- Document any paid tool justification

### SR-02: Platform Constraints
- Linux Mint as primary development platform
- REAPER for DAW testing
- C++17 minimum
- JUCE 8.0.x
- FetchContent for dependency management

### SR-03: Workflow Model
- Single developer + AI assistant (role-based-single-agent)
- Human makes all creative decisions
- AI handles implementation, research, boilerplate
- Session boundaries respect token limits

### SR-04: Timeline Considerations
- Multiple Claude sessions per feature expected
- Knowledge base population before heavy implementation
- Marketing activities before launch (30+ days)

